# Local Postgres only. This project holds synthetic data and must never be
# pointed at a cloud database, in tests or otherwise.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER@localhost:5432/clearpath_dev?connection_limit=10&pool_timeout=20"
SHADOW_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER@localhost:5432/clearpath_shadow"

# Keys the hash of a public-enquiry submitter's address, so the throttle table
# holds no recoverable list of who enquired. Names only — never a real value in
# a tracked file.
#
# Unset in production it throws, the same shape as CLEARPATH_BASE_URL below: a
# per-process random key would still keep the hashes unrecoverable, but on a
# platform where every request can land on a different instance that would
# throttle each instance separately rather than refuse loudly. Optional
# locally, where a per-process random is fine.
CLEARPATH_THROTTLE_SECRET=""

# One shared password over the whole site, HTTP Basic (SEC-01). Unset in
# production the site answers 503 to everything except /api/cron/*, on purpose:
# a deployment that forgot it must not be quietly public. Unset locally = no
# gate. Names only.
DEMO_ACCESS_PASSWORD=""

# Signs the break-glass cookie (SEC-03), so a hand-set cookie cannot open
# break-glass without the audit row startBreakGlass writes. Unset in production
# it throws, the same shape as CLEARPATH_THROTTLE_SECRET. Optional locally.
# Names only.
CLEARPATH_SESSION_SECRET=""

# Vercel Cron sends this as a bearer on /api/cron/reminders, /api/cron/purge and
# /api/cron/nonresponse.
# Unset, all three refuse every call — the schedule then runs nothing, so set
# it in the deployment's environment. Names only.
CRON_SECRET=""

# The host every client-facing link points at — the portal door in a reminder,
# the form link in a request. Unset in a production deployment, the link cannot
# be built and the run stops, on purpose: a queued link is unrecallable and a
# wrong one reports success all the way to a client's thumb.
#
# Optional on Vercel, where it falls back to VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL —
# the project's own production domain, custom domain included. Set it to
# override that, and set it in any command pointed at the deployed database:
# `db:seed:prod` is a local run with no NODE_ENV, and CLEARPATH_ALLOW_CLOUD_DB
# is what makes it refuse rather than quietly write localhost links into
# production. Names only.
CLEARPATH_BASE_URL=""

# Not set here, on purpose — `src/env.ts` validates them, but nothing in this
# file should hand you one. CLEARPATH_ALLOW_CLOUD_DB is typed by the db:*:prod
# scripts and means "I know this is a cloud database"; PORT defaults to 3700 in
# package.json; VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL comes from the platform.
